Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 19:19:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(inline): cap LLM call under Telegram's 10s inline-answer
 window
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the user types @<bot> <query> in a chat, Telegram drops the
inline answer if the bot doesn't respond within ~10s. Our previous
inline handler awaited llm.chat() with no per-call timeout, and
chat() walks the full model fallback chain (4 models on the default
Gemini config) with 3 exponential-backoff retries per model and a
45s request timeout. In the worst case that's many minutes — well
past Telegram's window, so the popup just sat empty and the user
saw 'inline doesn't work'.

Fix:
- Pin inline calls to the primary model only (skip the fallback chain).
- Add an 'attempts' parameter to LLMClient.chat() so callers can
  disable the retry loop (inline uses attempts=1).
- Wrap the call in asyncio.wait_for(timeout=8.0) — a hard cap under
  the 10s Telegram deadline.
- On timeout, return a clear 'не успела ответить, попробуй ещё раз'
  result with cache_time=0 so the user can retry immediately.
- Lower max_tokens to 200 for faster generation (replies are 1–3
  sentences anyway).
- Set cache_time=30 on successful answers (was 5) and 0 on errors
  (was 5) — caching the empty-query placeholder briefly is fine but
  caching error results made retries frustrating.

Also adds a regression test that uses a deliberately slow mock LLM
and verifies the handler returns a timeout result instead of hanging.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
